From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:19:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 107/160] hjviewer: review fixes, core2 lane (1.9)

TV-W3 (view-only Yes): the PC still ignores the upstream No that every
view-only switch sends, but takes the Yes sent on leaving view-only with
"lock after session end" on as "always", for same-account and other
sessions, as upstream and 1.8.x PCs lock.

TV-W3 (D4, reconnect): "another remote screen session" leaves out older
connections of the same session key that a reconnect replaced; the last
connection of a session does the locking, as upstream's.

TV-W3 (X-19 gap): the phone's switch to file transfer now sends
HJV_END_LOCK_SWITCH (proto value 4, additive) with upstream No. The PC does
not lock on that close and keeps the lock the mode would have made on the
session key's line, also past the 10 minutes. A remote screen that comes
back drops it and judges at its own end; otherwise the PC locks 30 s after
the session's last connection ended with none of it left (an automatic
lock is dropped while another controller's remote screen is open).

TV-W5: a cut forces the end lock only for an authorized connection; a
proven connection still waiting for its 2FA code is only cut.

hjv-e2e: a close reason from the PC ends a desktop session with exit code
7; 6 keeps "no ticket came" and "denied".

TV-W3 (controller): an own PC without a kept mode shows "always" when
upstream's switch is on, as the PC applies it; the kept mode is read once
per session (its PeerInfo), not once per process. The 'hide the screen when
connecting' switch can be turned off when the PC does not allow privacy
mode. The switch's own successful attempt no longer opens upstream's
"Enter privacy mode" box at every connection.

Tests: the uninstaller test has its doc comment back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
